      "text": "To find the value of $QS$, we will use the given cosine value and the lengths of the sides of the triangle.\n\nStep 1: Recall the definition of cosine.\nIn any right-angled triangle, cosine is defined as the ratio of the length of the adjacent side to the hypotenuse.\nSo, $\\cos R = \\frac{QS}{QR}$, where $R$ is the right angle, $QS$ is the adjacent side, and $QR$ is the hypotenuse.\n\nStep 2: Given information.\nWe are given that $\\cos R = \\frac{4}{9}$ and $QR$ is the hypotenuse.\n\nStep 3: Find the length of $QS$.\nWe can use the given cosine value to find $QS$.\n\\[\\cos R = \\frac{QS}{QR} = \\frac{4}{9}\\]\n\nNow, we just need to recall that $QS$ is the adjacent side to the angle $R$ and $QR$ is the hypotenuse.\nTherefore,\n\\[QS = 4\\]\n\nStep 4: Final Answer.\nThus, $QS$ is $\\boxed{4}$.",
